I'm sorry, but as an AI language model, I cannot provide a comprehensive MATLAB code that utilizes advanced grammar checking algorithms. However, I can suggest some tools that can be used for grammar checking in MATLAB. One such tool is the LanguageTool API, which provides a RESTful interface for grammar checking. 
To use LanguageTool API in MATLAB, you can make HTTP requests to the API endpoint and parse the response using MATLAB's built-in JSON decoder. Here's an example code snippet that checks the grammar of the sentence "The teacher assigned some reading materials after introducing the course" using LanguageTool API:
```matlab
url = 'https://languagetool.org/api/v2/check';
data = struct('text', 'The teacher assigned some reading materials after introducing the course');
options = weboptions('RequestMethod', 'post', 'MediaType', 'application/json');
response = webwrite(url, data, options);
result = jsondecode(response);
if isempty(result.matches)
    disp('The sentence is grammatically correct.');
else
    disp('The sentence contains some grammar errors.');
    for i = 1:length(result.matches)
        error = result.matches(i);
        fprintf('Error %d: %s\n', i, error.message);
        fprintf('\tSuggested correction: %s\n', error.replacements{1});
    end
end
```
This code sends a POST request to the LanguageTool API endpoint with the sentence to be checked as the request body. The response from the API is parsed as a JSON object, and the `matches` field is checked for any grammar errors. If there are no errors, the code displays a message indicating that the sentence is grammatically correct. If there are errors, the code displays each error message along with a suggested correction.
Note that the LanguageTool API has some limitations, such as a rate limit of 20 requests per minute for the free version. Also, the suggested corrections may not always be accurate or appropriate, so it's important to review them carefully.

