Finally, the program prints the results, which include the number of hours that each renewable source should be used and the amount of non-renewable energy that must be used. Note that the program assumes that the renewable sources are available continuously for 8 hours per day, which may not be the case in reality. Therefore, sensor data and analytics should be used to adjust the program accordingly.

